WEBVTT

00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:23,100
My oncologist is recommended I do genetic testing using a blood sample to possibly find more treatment options. Have you heard of effective or safe treatments resulting from these tests.

00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:33,100
Yes, for sure that there are different genetic issues that

00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:44,100
can suggest a specific treatment option from standards of care. So if they're recommended you do that and

00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:59,100
and you have and they're paying for it and your chance is covering that. I've always said if they're going to do a full genetic workup on you because it's going to be different than what we did on you if we if we did the genetic workup on you.

00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:13,100
They're going to be looking for tumor suppressor genes and they're looking for specific genes that are being studied for specific treatment pathways and if you're open to doing standards of care that might open another doorway.

00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:20,100
So if they're going to, if it's going to be covered under your insurance, I for sure go for that and do that. Yes.

